WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.630
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Daniel. Welcome to Online Intermediate.

2
00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:08.177
Hi! I'm Nita. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.477 --> 00:00:15.112
Unit thirty-two: Learning Languages. In this unit, you will talk about language learning and check information politely.

4
00:00:16.117 --> 00:00:16.920
fluent.

5
00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:20.746
fluent means able to speak a language easily and well.

6
00:00:21.046 --> 00:00:25.112
After two years in Japan, he became fluent in Japanese.

7
00:00:25.812 --> 00:00:27.826
Your turn. Say: fluent.

8
00:00:30.526 --> 00:00:31.318
fluent.

9
00:00:32.317 --> 00:00:33.213
accent.

10
00:00:33.913 --> 00:00:37.039
accent means the way people from a place pronounce words.

11
00:00:37.339 --> 00:00:39.907
She speaks English with a lovely Khmer accent.

12
00:00:40.607 --> 00:00:42.586
Your turn. Say: accent.

13
00:00:45.286 --> 00:00:46.218
accent.

14
00:00:47.217 --> 00:00:48.264
vocabulary.

15
00:00:48.964 --> 00:00:52.694
vocabulary means all the words in a language that a person knows.

16
00:00:52.994 --> 00:00:55.307
Reading helps you build your vocabulary.

17
00:00:56.007 --> 00:00:58.322
Your turn. Say: vocabulary.

18
00:01:01.022 --> 00:01:02.198
vocabulary.

19
00:01:03.183 --> 00:01:04.254
grammar rule.

20
00:01:04.954 --> 00:01:08.405
grammar rule means a rule about how words are used in sentences.

21
00:01:08.705 --> 00:01:10.983
This grammar rule has many exceptions.

22
00:01:11.683 --> 00:01:13.894
Your turn. Say: grammar rule.

23
00:01:16.594 --> 00:01:17.607
grammar rule.

24
00:01:18.617 --> 00:01:19.687
pronunciation.

25
00:01:20.387 --> 00:01:23.246
pronunciation means the way a word is said.

26
00:01:23.546 --> 00:01:26.672
The pronunciation of 'th' is difficult for many learners.

27
00:01:27.372 --> 00:01:29.769
Your turn. Say: pronunciation.

28
00:01:32.469 --> 00:01:33.574
pronunciation.

29
00:01:34.583 --> 00:01:35.666
native speaker.

30
00:01:36.366 --> 00:01:39.596
native speaker means a person who learned a language as a child.

31
00:01:39.896 --> 00:01:42.871
Practising with a native speaker helps your listening.

32
00:01:43.571 --> 00:01:46.002
Your turn. Say: native speaker.

33
00:01:48.702 --> 00:01:49.982
native speaker.

34
00:01:50.983 --> 00:01:51.903
bilingual.

35
00:01:52.603 --> 00:01:55.543
bilingual means able to speak two languages very well.

36
00:01:55.843 --> 00:01:58.539
Their children are bilingual in Khmer and English.

37
00:01:59.239 --> 00:02:01.392
Your turn. Say: bilingual.

38
00:02:04.092 --> 00:02:04.908
bilingual.

39
00:02:05.917 --> 00:02:07.196
language exchange.

40
00:02:07.896 --> 00:02:12.032
language exchange means meeting someone to practise each other's languages.

41
00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:15.295
I do a language exchange with a French student every week.

42
00:02:15.995 --> 00:02:18.683
Your turn. Say: language exchange.

43
00:02:21.383 --> 00:02:22.778
language exchange.

44
00:02:23.783 --> 00:02:26.201
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:26.501 --> 00:02:28.187
You've improved a lot, haven't you?

46
00:02:29.483 --> 00:02:33.726
I hope so! I do a language exchange every Saturday, don't I?

47
00:02:35.017 --> 00:02:38.026
Yes, with a native speaker from Canada, isn't it?

48
00:02:39.317 --> 00:02:42.967
That's right. My pronunciation is better now, isn't it?

49
00:02:44.283 --> 00:02:46.831
It is. Your vocabulary has grown too.

50
00:02:48.117 --> 00:02:51.477
I want to be fluent one day. That's possible, isn't it?

51
00:02:52.783 --> 00:02:55.062
Grammar focus: Question tags.

52
00:02:55.362 --> 00:02:58.801
Use question tags to check information or ask for agreement.

53
00:02:59.101 --> 00:03:04.177
A positive sentence has a negative tag, and a negative sentence has a positive tag.

54
00:03:04.477 --> 00:03:08.987
For example: You speak French, don't you? She isn't a native speaker, is she?

55
00:03:09.287 --> 00:03:16.395
Use the same auxiliary verb as the sentence: is → isn't, have → haven't, present simple → do / does.

56
00:03:17.383 --> 00:03:19.978
Now read and listen. How to Become Fluent.

57
00:03:20.278 --> 00:03:23.775
Becoming fluent in a language takes time and regular practice.

58
00:03:25.083 --> 00:03:27.559
Many learners worry too much about their accent.

59
00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:33.160
In fact, clear pronunciation is more important than sounding like a native speaker.

60
00:03:34.450 --> 00:03:38.667
Learning ten new words a day can double your vocabulary in a year.

61
00:03:39.983 --> 00:03:43.272
A language exchange is a fun and free way to practise speaking.

62
00:03:44.583 --> 00:03:46.957
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

63
00:03:47.257 --> 00:03:50.034
Able to speak two languages very well is blank.

64
00:03:50.334 --> 00:03:53.210
A, fluent. B, bilingual. C, accent.

65
00:03:57.217 --> 00:03:58.891
The answer is B: bilingual.

66
00:04:00.383 --> 00:04:01.721
You're a student, blank?

67
00:04:02.021 --> 00:04:04.978
A, are you. B, aren't you. C, don't you.

68
00:04:08.983 --> 00:04:10.774
The answer is B: aren't you.

69
00:04:12.283 --> 00:04:13.969
He doesn't like coffee, blank?

70
00:04:14.269 --> 00:04:17.551
A, does he. B, doesn't he. C, is he.

71
00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:23.062
The answer is A: does he.

72
00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:26.642
The way a word is said is its blank.

73
00:04:26.942 --> 00:04:30.933
A, vocabulary. B, pronunciation. C, grammar rule.

74
00:04:34.917 --> 00:04:37.137
The answer is B: pronunciation.

75
00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:42.821
According to the text, what is more important than sounding like a native speaker?

76
00:04:43.121 --> 00:04:47.250
A, clear pronunciation. B, fast speaking. C, perfect grammar.

77
00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:53.760
The answer is A: clear pronunciation.

78
00:04:55.250 --> 00:04:59.156
Now it's your turn to speak. What is the best way to learn a new language?

79
00:05:04.456 --> 00:05:10.847
Practise every day, read a lot and find a language exchange partner. Speaking is the key, isn't it?

80
00:05:11.147 --> 00:05:12.682
Excellent answer, Nita!

81
00:05:13.683 --> 00:05:17.415
Great work today! You learned eight new words and question tags.

82
00:05:17.715 --> 00:05:21.204
Today's value is pride in learning. Be proud of what you learned.

83
00:05:21.504 --> 00:05:23.959
See you in Unit thirty-three. Goodbye!

84
00:05:24.259 --> 00:05:26.748
Thank you, Mr. Daniel! Bye, everyone!

